     },
     {
      "id": "st",
      "text": "Stable",
      "why": "$\\Delta < 0$ gives a positive eigenvalue."
     },
     {
      "id": "deg",
      "text": "Degenerate",
      "why": "$\\Delta = -1 \\ne 0$."
     }
    ],
    "shuffle": true
   },
   "feedback": {
    "correct": "$\\Delta = -1 < 0$: a saddle, whatever $\\tau$ is.",
    "generic": "Not quite right. Compute $\\Delta$ before reading $\\tau$."
   },
   "explain": {
    "text": "Eigenvalues $\\pm 1$: real and of opposite sign. $\\tau = 0$ means a centre only when $\\Delta > 0$."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "r-damping-system",
   "difficulty": 3,
   "skills": [
    "de-systems",
    "de-second"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "trace-det"
   ],
   "prose": "Recall lesson 9: $y'' + 2y' + 5y = 0$. As a system, $\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-5&-2\\end{pmatrix}$.",
   "question": "Where is it on the trace-determinant map?",
   "widget": {
    "kind": "choice",
    "layout": "stack",
    "options": [
     {
      "id": "ss",
      "text": "$(-2, 5)$, a stable spiral: under-damped",
      "correct": true
     },
     {
      "id": "sn",
      "text": "$(-2, 5)$, a stable node: over-damped",
      "why": "$\\tau^2 = 4 < 20 = 4\\Delta$: inside the parabola, a spiral."
     },
     {
      "id": "crit",
      "text": "On the parabola: critical",
      "why": "Critical would need $b^2 = 20$."
     },
     {
      "id": "sad",
      "text": "$(-2, -5)$, a saddle",
      "why": "$\\Delta = 0 \\cdot (-2) - (1)(-5) = +5$."
     }
    ],
    "shuffle": true
   },
   "feedback": {
    "correct": "$\\tau = -2$, $\\Delta = 5$: inside the parabola, so it rings.",
    "generic": "Not quite right. Compute $\\tau$ and $\\Delta$, then compare $\\tau^2$ with $4\\Delta$."
   },
   "explain": {
    "text": "Under-damped oscillators are stable spirals in the phase plane; $\\lambda = -1 \\pm 2i$."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "r-linearise",
   "difficulty": 4,
   "skills": [
    "de-systems"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "linearise"
   ],
   "prose": "Take $x' = x(1 - x) - xy$, $y' = y(x - 0.5)$. The positive equilibrium is $(0.5, 0.5)$, where $\\mathbf{J} = \\begin{pmatrix}-0.5&-0.5\\\\0.5&0\\end{pmatrix}$.",
   "question": "Which type is it?",
   "widget": {
    "kind": "choice",
    "layout": "stack",
    "options": [
     {
      "id": "ss",
      "text": "Stable spiral",
      "correct": true
     },
     {
      "id": "sn",
      "text": "Stable node",
      "why": "$\\tau^2 = 0.25 < 1 = 4\\Delta$: a spiral."
     },
     {
      "id": "c",
      "text": "Centre",
      "why": "$\\tau = -0.5 \\ne 0$."
     },
     {
      "id": "sad",
      "text": "Saddle",
      "why": "$\\Delta = 0.25 > 0$."
     }
    ],
    "shuffle": true
   },
   "feedback": {
    "correct": "$\\tau = -0.5$, $\\Delta = 0.25$: $\\lambda = -0.25 \\pm 0.433i$.",
    "generic": "Not quite right. Compute $\\tau$, $\\Delta$ and $\\tau^2 - 4\\Delta$."
   },
   "explain": {
    "text": "$\\tau^2 - 4\\Delta = -0.75 < 0$ and $\\tau < 0$: a stable spiral, trusted for the nonlinear system near the point."
   }
  },
